<title>UK: UK's Clarke says increasing spending on schools.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says increasing spending on schools.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday that UK spending on schools would rise by an extra 830 million pounds in 1997.</p>
<p>Clarke said in his budget presentation that 878 million pounds of extra money for schools was provided this year.</p>
<p>He said 633 million pounds of the new money for 1997 would be channelled through local authorities.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
